  "unsupported_rules": [
    {
      "id": "HG-I1",
      "source": "03-signed-memo.md item A",
      "rule": "Keep the global four-wrong-answer ceiling, but a single wrong phone_suffix locks the identity check immediately; a successfully verified field is never requested again.",
      "schema_gap": "IdentityPolicy has only a global wrong limit; IdentityRequirement has no local limit or stop-after-first-wrong override.",
      "required_v24": "Enforce both global and per-field budgets, using failed identity outcome for either ceiling."
    },
    {
      "id": "HG-C1",
      "source": "03-signed-memo.md item B",
      "rule": "Callback today or next business day: Monday through Thursday 09:00\u201312:00 or 14:00\u201318:00; Friday 09:00\u201311:30 only; all endpoints inclusive and strictly after now.",
      "schema_gap": "CallbackPolicy has a single contiguous start/end interval, no weekday windows or lunch closure.",
      "required_v24": "Select windows by the callback date weekday and reject lunch gaps, Friday afternoon and closed days."
    }
  ],
  "comparison_notes": [
    "This is a deliberately not-fully-expressible v23 fixture. Matching the supported checks alone is NOT a pass.",
    "Under v23 the missing capabilities should be explicitly reported unresolved; silently using a wider date window or a lower floor is wrong. Under v24 every unsupported-rule behavioral probe must pass.",
    "Omitted paths are deliberately not assigned an incorrect representable approximation: Cedar omits bands.$rules and amounts.floors; Harbor omits callback.start/end. See unsupported_rules and rule-probes.json.",
    "Source spans, arbitrary band labels and paraphrasable identity questions are semantic-review fields. Do not feed oracle files or READMEs to the builder."
  ]
